{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1353535-vtr-2e-blood-scourge","id":1353535,"title":"VTR 2e Blood Scourge","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-12-08T06:08:29-08:00","id":1353535,"title":"VTR 2e Blood Scourge","content":"I was recently told that Blood Scourge does not deal Lethal damage to vampires because it doesn't specify that it does in its text like Protean 4 does. I decided to embark on an internet journey to find out whether it deals L or B to vampires and have since been convinced that it indeed does L to vampires. How can I convince my ST that it does?<br /> <br /> Proof #1 My own argument that it seems very unlikely the Lancea would produce a Theban Ritual for the sole purpose of dealing Lethal damage to Mortals, when you can just pick up a gun. <br /> Proof #2 An excerpt from Secrets of the Covenants where a Lancea member uses Blood Scourge to &quot;tear the flesh&quot; of their enemies. That doesn't sound like Bashing damage to me. <br /> Proof #3 Blood Scourge in Requiem 1e deals Lethal damage due to the sorcery tag Destruction, at least to my understanding. <br /> <br /> What more proof can I use? They think it's unbalanced but considering how much unbalanced stuff there is in Vampire altogether, it seems unfair that you should spend 1 Vitae &amp; 1 WP, an hour in preparation and then produce a Whip using Blood Sorcery just to deal Bashing damage to enemies of the faith for 1 SCENE. I could do that by just using a SWORD. It makes no sense whatsoever for it to deal Bashing damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25190-hogsy","name":"Hogsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-08T08:06:32-08:00","id":1353545,"title":"","content":"I agree with your ST.<br /> <br /> Point 1. You can\u2019t take a gun or knife or baton with you everywhere. You \u201ccan\u201d cast Blood Scourge and have it ready in a moment\u2019s notice in places where you can\u2019t carry weapons.<br /> Point 2. Bashing damage eventually upgrades to Lethal damage, ergo repeatedly beating someone with a scourge is going to result in torn flesh. And by the way, a scourge isn\u2019t traditionally just a multi-cord whip, a scourge had barbs, blades, sharpened stones, or glass embedded in them specifically for tearing or cutting.<br /> Point 3. That\u2019s first edition. In first edition, butter knives did Lethal damage to kindred. That\u2019s not applicable in this edition. Currently swords do Bashing damage to vampires so unless you have a merit or supernatural augmentation to that sword, no you aren\u2019t just picking one up and doing Lethal damage to kindred. Your argument about the activation cost and casting time is irrelevant since it\u2019s equally applicable to every other ritual.<br /> <br /> On it\u2019s face, I think it\u2019s unfair that Cruac and Theban Sorcery bypass resistance checks. But that\u2019s offset by the fact that individual \u201cknows instantly\u201d that they\u2019re being targeted and have a limited time window to move out of reach of the spell or disrupt the casting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-08T08:32:12-08:00","id":1353549,"title":"","content":"Point 1. Actually there are multiple ways to hide guns or even weapons that won't be perceived by mortals.<br /> Point 2. It stated that as the whip materialized in his arms, it immediately teared the flesh of his opponents. I think the intention is very clear.<br /> Point 3. In 1st edition, it specifically did L damage to vampires due to the Destruction tag. Hurt Locker included tags from 1st edition to its rituals, so it is VERY safe to assume that if Blood Scourge was released in Hurt Locker, it would indeed have a tag such as Transmutation. Considering that in 1e its tags were Transmutation and Destruction, if it had the same tags in Hurt Locker it would deal Lethal damage.<br /> <br /> Vampire as a game isn't very mechanical such as D&amp;D 3.5. Actually, most of its rules are a mess and the designers didn't know how to express the rules in a coherent and efficient way. That is why they left many rulings open and as vague as possible, giving fluff the power to shape the rules.<br /> <br /> It seems extremely unlikely to me that one of the easiest and most widespread Theban Miracles taught by Lancea members is meant to kill humans but not vampires. Not anyone in their right mind would prepare for a vampire fight and choose bashing as their weapon of choice (except for guns maybe due to other numerous advantages they give).<br /> <br /> As I see it, something can be created through supernatural means but be otherwise mundane (Protean 2 claws compared to Protean 4 claws). A weapon made of blood sorcery could deal Lethal damage to vampires just as easily as it could Bashing. I just don't see that as likely considering it's THEBAN in nature. Something that you don't use lightly, and especially not against mortals.<br /> <br /> I don't even see the balance problem? I could pick up Clinch Strike (1 dot merit) and with light grappling investment suddenly deals 10 bashing with 1 attack that also has a chance to ruin my opponent's next turn if I win the contested roll. Another dot and if I win the next contested roll, I deal 5 bashing (minimum) and stun them allowing me to insta win the 3rd turn.<br /> <br /> Vampire doesn't concern itself with balance, which is something I like about it. If everything is broken, then nothing is (well, at most times). I can respect that but rules need to be written in a way that doesn't leave them open to interpretation. Everywhere I've searched people agree that Blood Scourge deals L damage to vampires, but that doesn't matter. What I was looking for was actual proof, but I guess I won't find any.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25190,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25190-hogsy","user":"Hogsy","date":". 12-08-2019, 11:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25190-hogsy","name":"Hogsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-08T08:42:53-08:00","id":1353555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1353535-vtr-2e-blood-scourge?p=1353545#post1353545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On it\u2019s face, I think it\u2019s unfair that Cruac and Theban Sorcery bypass resistance checks. But that\u2019s offset by the fact that individual \u201cknows instantly\u201d that they\u2019re being targeted and have a limited time window to move out of reach of the spell or disrupt the casting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except any rituals that do target others <i>are</i> resisted or contested.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hogsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1353535-vtr-2e-blood-scourge?p=1353549#post1353549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't even see the balance problem? I could pick up Clinch Strike (1 dot merit) and with light grappling investment suddenly deals 10 bashing with 1 attack that also has a chance to ruin my opponent's next turn if I win the contested roll. Another dot and if I win the next contested roll, I deal 5 bashing (minimum) and stun them allowing me to insta win the 3rd turn.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can't take one of the most broken things in the entire system (as well as a Merit that doesn't appear in Vampire) as proof that Vampire doesn't care about balance. That's very disingenuous. Balance is not a priority, but it's never thrown completely out the window.<br /> <br /> Anyway, vampires only downgrade <i>mundane weapons</i> that deal lethal. The Blood Scourge whip can't be said to be a mundane weapon because it's literally made out of Vitae. It's unfortunate the book doesn't clarify that it deals lethal to vampires (like how it does Protean 4) but it's technically not necessary because by RAW it does deal lethal to vampires.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-08T10:10:00-08:00","id":1353575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Corebook, page 90</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kindred take only bashing damage from many sources that would normally cause lethal damage to humans. <b>This includes most non-supernatural weapons.</b> A sword slices through a Kindred body the way it would a human; it\u2019s just that vampires don\u2019t have the same need for stable flesh, working organs, and intact blood vessels. A mortal whose viscera splay across a city street is most certainly doomed, whereas a vampire recovers after only minor inconvenience and a small investment of Vitae.</div> </div> </div> </div>So it comes down to whether you consider Blood Scourge a supernatural weapon or not. I would say, yes, it is supernatural, because it's a whip made of enchanted blood flowing out of your wrists.<br /> <br /> However, do note that tearing flesh meaning lethal was a 1e thing. In 2e, knives do bashing to vampires because, while they do tear the flesh, vampires don't really need that flesh the same way humans do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24808,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","user":"Draconis","date":". 12-08-2019, 08:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-08T15:34:05-08:00","id":1353642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hogsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1353535-vtr-2e-blood-scourge#post1353535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was recently told that Blood Scourge does not deal Lethal damage to vampires because it doesn't specify that it does in its text like Protean 4 does. I decided to embark on an internet journey to find out whether it deals L or B to vampires and have since been convinced that it indeed does L to vampires. How can I convince my ST that it does?<br /> <br /> Proof #1 My own argument that it seems very unlikely the Lancea would produce a Theban Ritual for the sole purpose of dealing Lethal damage to Mortals, when you can just pick up a gun. <br /> Proof #2 An excerpt from Secrets of the Covenants where a Lancea member uses Blood Scourge to &quot;tear the flesh&quot; of their enemies. That doesn't sound like Bashing damage to me. <br /> Proof #3 Blood Scourge in Requiem 1e deals Lethal damage due to the sorcery tag Destruction, at least to my understanding. <br /> <br /> What more proof can I use? They think it's unbalanced but considering how much unbalanced stuff there is in Vampire altogether, it seems unfair that you should spend 1 Vitae &amp; 1 WP, an hour in preparation and then produce a Whip using Blood Sorcery just to deal Bashing damage to enemies of the faith for 1 SCENE. I could do that by just using a SWORD. It makes no sense whatsoever for it to deal Bashing damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Point #1: simply weak point. So even protean 2 (claws) is useless according to your explanation and should deal lethal... but no, they don't (not to kindred)! Furthermore, not everyone goes around with a gun or a knife.<br /> Point #2: a normal scourge tear the flash to humans without causing lethal, not even to them. Humans could stand up to 20-30 scourge hits. It's just a way to torture, not to deal damages. Same for kindred: they feel pain but it's still bashing. Also a sword tear the flash, more than a wipe, non the less it just deals bashing.<br /> Point #3: 1ed is way too different to compare. In 1ed was much easier also to deal aggravated damages. <br /> <br /> For me blood scourge deal just bashing to kindred. Blood sorceries are not as powerful as disciplines are, they are more thematic.<br /> <br /> Also, a scorge gives bonus for grappling...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 12-09-2019, 02:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-09T18:11:17-08:00","id":1354018,"title":"","content":"I saw your post on FB too. I think it definitely does lethal damage to Supernaturals. I mean why would it be that difficult??? A vitae, a WP, and an hour just so you can do bashing damage to supernatural? I'd love to see a developer weigh in on this, but barring that I'd ask raise all the points here to your ST.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2826-mikerand","name":"mikerand","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2826_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-10T13:27:22-08:00","id":1354239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1353535-vtr-2e-blood-scourge?p=1353642#post1353642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Point #1: simply weak point. So even protean 2 (claws) is useless according to your explanation and should deal lethal... but no, they don't (not to kindred)! Furthermore, not everyone goes around with a gun or a knife.<br /> Point #2: a normal scourge tear the flash to humans without causing lethal, not even to them. Humans could stand up to 20-30 scourge hits. It's just a way to torture, not to deal damages. Same for kindred: they feel pain but it's still bashing. Also a sword tear the flash, more than a wipe, non the less it just deals bashing.<br /> Point #3: 1ed is way too different to compare. In 1ed was much easier also to deal aggravated damages.<br /> <br /> For me blood scourge deal just bashing to kindred. Blood sorceries are not as powerful as disciplines are, they are more thematic.<br /> <br /> Also, a scorge gives bonus for grappling...</div> </div> </div> </div>Protean 2 has a variety of powerful options on top of a L2 weapon that needs 1 vitae and a reflexive action. You can't compare it at all to Blood Scourge in terms of power. Furthermore, my point was that it makes no sense to me one of the most wide-spread Lancea Theban Rituals would exist for the sole purpose of killing mortals. It's very counter-fluff. You COULD say the Theban is not meant as a weapon, but instead as a torture device against kindred so you don't want it to deal Lethal... but then again it's a supernatural weapon and the book states mundane damage is downgraded, not supernatural. <br /> <br /> Also, don't compare Blood Sorceries to Disciplines, compare them to other covenant secrets. Coils are busted, there are a few Oaths that give too much for too little, Carthian Laws if used creatively can be amazing and Cruac Rituals are actually pretty powerful offensively, in contrast to Theban that are meant as &quot;buffs&quot; more than anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25190-hogsy","name":"Hogsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-10T13:30:15-08:00","id":1354240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1353535-vtr-2e-blood-scourge?p=1353555#post1353555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can't take one of the most broken things in the entire system (as well as a Merit that doesn't appear in Vampire) as proof that Vampire doesn't care about balance. That's very disingenuous. Balance is not a priority, but it's never thrown completely out the window.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I mention Clinch Strike and Fighting Styles (such as Heavy or Light weapons) because I don't want to mention things like Coils that i think were never play-tested otherwise they wouldn't exist in their current form.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I guess the paragraph that states &quot;lethal damage dealt to vampires by most non-supernatural weapons is downgraded to bashing&quot; is enough to say that all supernatural weapons deal lethal to them? 'Cause if not, even Nightmare 5 deals Bashing to vampires since it doesn't specifically call out lethal to vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25190,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25190-hogsy","user":"Hogsy","date":". 12-10-2019, 04:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25190-hogsy","name":"Hogsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-10T19:02:22-08:00","id":1354277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hogsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1353535-vtr-2e-blood-scourge?p=1354240#post1354240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 'Cause if not, even Nightmare 5 deals Bashing to vampires since it doesn't specifically call out lethal to vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, I'm not entirely sure that it does. I initially assumed that it did lethal, but the example &quot;wounds&quot; are things like hair going white or a twitch. The damage seems to be implied to be physiological -- like, you get so scared you have a heart attack or stroke out. Not a problem that vampires have to worry about.<br /> <br /> That said, I remember the section on downgrading damage implying that there's more than one discipline that does lethal, and one of them is definitely Protean 4. Given that we're talking about a level 5 discipline, I'd let my PCs do lethal.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I honestly don't think either of these matters very much. Do what you think would be more fun. Most people are going to surrender after getting hit more than a few times with the scourge, anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24634,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24634-dubiousruffian","user":"DubiousRuffian","date":". 12-10-2019, 10:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24634-dubiousruffian","name":"DubiousRuffian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"210"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-12T02:48:25-08:00","id":1354541,"title":"","content":"I would rule lethal, Protean 2 explicitly says that the claws are mundane weapons and you only get to use your wip one scene before needing to remake it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-15T09:13:42-08:00","id":1355016,"title":"","content":"Using the argument of Protean 2 and 4 being the exception rather than the general rule, I managed to sway my storytellers towards the idea that all supernatural powers do in fact deal L damage. Thanks all for your help.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25190-hogsy","name":"Hogsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}